    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Moulded By Industry is William D. Drake’s sixth solo album and his first in a decade, released by Onomatopoeia Records. Drawing on his history with Cardiacs and The Sea Nymphs, Drake combines Mellotron-rich grandeur, intricate piano-led composition, art-rock eccentricity, and pop-minded melody. The nine-track set returns to the richly layered, expansive production associated with Briny Hooves, while retaining his characteristically surreal and playful sensibility.\n\nThe album sets poetry by John Clare and Thomas Ashe alongside Drake’s own writing, giving songs such as “Green Shadows,” “Turtledove,” “The Storm,” and “Distant Hills” an evocative pastoral atmosphere shaped by love, longing, loss, and the English countryside. Longtime collaborators James Larcombe, Dean Gaisburgh-Watkyn, and Steve Jackson are joined by singer Treana Morris, contributing to the record’s dense yet emotionally intimate sound. Critics have described it as challenging, strange, and deeply moving—a distinctive work that turns old texts and ornate arrangements into something vivid and contemporary.",
